The portable C in the scenario second-copy: what it is expected to show
otherwise than the original. A patch of harness/goldens/second-copy.txt, see
harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the golden's, a line with + is what is
expected in its place.
Deviation: 1, 10 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: the second copy has no memory to run a command: each copy keeps all of
itself. And by 10, the box of F10 names the program in its title and in its
question, by a name that is two letters shorter: the box is two cells
narrower, a cell on either side, and its shadow ends a cell further left

